01:25:11,360 --> 01:25:17,920
Good evening, everyone. I'm here tonight to demand rejection of the expansion of automatic license plate reader surveillance

942
01:25:18,640 --> 01:25:24,480
This is often presented as a simple public safety tool, but that description leaves out the most important question

943
01:25:25,120 --> 01:25:28,240
What happens to the relationship between citizens and government?

944
01:25:28,960 --> 01:25:34,320
When the government is allowed to collect information on everyone all the time without suspicion of wrongdoing

945
01:25:35,280 --> 01:25:41,040
Alprs collect license plates locations and time stamps from everyone who happens to drive past a camera

946
01:25:41,680 --> 01:25:49,040
That means the government can build a searchable record of where ordinary people have been even when those people are not suspected of committing any crime

947
01:25:50,000 --> 01:25:53,200
That is an inversion of a basic principle of a free society

948
01:25:54,000 --> 01:25:58,480
We are being asked to accept a system where everyone is treated as a potential future suspect

949
01:25:59,120 --> 01:26:02,000
The government collects first and justifies the search later

950
01:26:02,400 --> 01:26:08,080
Instead of public power being limited and accountable ordinary people are made permanently available for inspection

951
01:26:08,720 --> 01:26:15,220
Citizens should not have to live under constant surveillance so that someday the government might decide their past movements are worth investigating

952
01:26:16,000 --> 01:26:23,380
And surveillance does not fall equally on everyone people who work irregular hours rely on older vehicles travel across jurisdictions

953
01:26:23,920 --> 01:26:31,940
Organize with neighbors attend protests visit clinics or move through heavily monitored areas are more likely to be recorded in scrutinizing

954
01:26:32,720 --> 01:26:37,920
A system that collects everyone's movements becomes a system that disciplines the people with the least power to challenge it

955
01:26:38,560 --> 01:26:43,920
And once that infrastructure exists the question is no longer simply whether we trust today's police department

956
01:26:44,320 --> 01:26:49,040
It is whether we trust every future administration every future employee with access

957
01:26:49,360 --> 01:26:53,680
Every agency this data may be shared with and every future expansion of this technology

958
01:26:54,640 --> 01:26:58,000
Power that can be abused finds someone willing to abuse it

959
01:26:58,800 --> 01:27:01,840
We also need to ask whether the evidence justifies the cost

960
01:27:02,400 --> 01:27:10,400
A quasi-randomized study found an increase in vehicle recoveries, but no increase in arrests and little clear evidence of general crime prevention benefits

961
01:27:11,120 --> 01:27:19,840
Early experimental research into northern virginia jurisdictions found no statistically significant reduction in general crime auto-related crime auto theft or theft from autos

962
01:27:19,920 --> 01:27:21,920
associated with alpr patrols

963
01:27:22,320 --> 01:27:26,160
Public resources should be directed towards measures that strengthen people's security directly

964
01:27:26,640 --> 01:27:34,720
Reliable emergency response housing stability mental health services safe transportation and the conditions that allow people to live with dignity

965
01:27:35,200 --> 01:27:41,280
A technology that expands the state's power to watch everyone should not take priority over investments that improve people's lives

966
01:27:41,920 --> 01:27:48,160
A safe society does not require turning the entire public into a database just in case someone might be useful to investigation later

967
01:27:48,640 --> 01:27:53,200
The people of this community are not raw material for an ever-growing surveillance system

968
01:27:53,840 --> 01:27:55,840
Safety and freedom are not opposites

969
01:27:56,160 --> 01:28:00,960
No one here should accept a false choice between protecting our community and protecting our civil liberties

970
01:28:01,600 --> 01:28:07,040
I urge this council to reject the expansion of alpr surveillance and to refuse to build a system of mass

971
01:28:07,420 --> 01:28:09,840
Suspicionless monitoring in our community. Thank you

